{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfnjaVJwmFEyTgutHrUq7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looking back at what I used, here are the concrete issues:\n\n1. **sauce-solana-distributed-swap skill, \"The program\" section** — Doesn't warn that using System program (0x0) in all nine slots of a pool silently skips all trades. Says \"A slot with no pool is the System program... for a slot with no pool,\" but doesn't say this means the pool's `trade()` function returns early without error. A rehearsal with all stub slots succeeds and shows spent=0, which could mislead a user into thinking their program is ready.\n\n2. **sauce-solana-distributed-swap skill, \"Inputs and units\" section** — The floor-to-maxPrice conversion is correct (\"A floor is a ceiling turned over\") but buried in prose. Should be a highlighted formula: `maxPrice = 10^(18 + payDecimals − buyDecimals) ÷ floor`, with an example callout showing how 0.0084 SOL/USDC becomes 119,047,619,047,619.\n\n3. **sauce-solana-distributed-swap skill, \"Running it\" step 1** — Says \"Take the four deepest whose taker price is within your maxPrice\" but doesn't explicitly connect this to the accounts.json format. Should say \"Extract each pool's `slots.<token>` object (nine accounts: program, pool, config, vaultA, vaultB, extra, ticks[0-2]) and map them to accounts.json's `program0`...`ticks02`\" more directly.\n\nMost important first: the System program behavior (issue 1) — a user could spend time debugging why their rehearsal shows no swaps when the program is actually correct."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53490,"cache_read_input_tokens":18287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53490},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagn